WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.929
Film Courage: Every creative person should
consider themselves primarily responsible

00:00:03.929 --> 00:00:05.540
for the success of their career?

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.479
Is this true?

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:12.210
Gary W. Goldstein: Is it an absolutely true
statement that every creative person needs

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:22.179
to be that primarily responsible person who
stewards their own career, who is the architect.

00:00:22.179 --> 00:00:28.650
It’s great if you have others with their
oars in the water helping you.

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:31.159
It’s great if you have an agent.

00:00:31.159 --> 00:00:34.180
It’s great if you have a manager, if you
have an attorney, if you have other people

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:41.900
who are mentors or wear different hats in
your life who contribute strategy, time, effort,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.270
money, whatever all those things are.

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:50.570
All contributions (smart and well-intended
contributions) are welcomed, of course.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:57.350
But the statement we hear so often from a
creative “If only I had an agent” is an

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.480
unfortunate statement in my view.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.280
Because even when you have one, you are still
100% responsible.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:08.310
When I was a personal manager representing
primarily writers and directors (some actors),

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:16.049
but when I was a literary manager my attitude
was first I had to deal with my writer.

00:01:16.049 --> 00:01:19.869
You work as hard at being a writer as I work
at being your representative and we’re going

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:20.990
to get along great.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:26.259
But, (by the way) you’re still 100 percent
responsible for your career.

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:30.969
And (by the way), so am I. I am 100 percent
responsible for your career.

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:34.829
And when we get you an agent, the agent is
100 percent responsible for your career.

00:01:34.829 --> 00:01:37.700
Now we’ve got 300 percent.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:41.750
Sounds like THE PRODUCERS, but it’s true.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:50.799
I could never allow anyone to be even 1 percent
responsible or I wasn’t giving my all.

00:01:50.799 --> 00:01:53.670
So when they get an agent, when they get a
manager, when they get people who want to

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:54.780
jump on board, that’s great.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.299
But it’s frosting, it’s not the cake.

00:01:56.299 --> 00:01:57.549
They have to be the one.

00:01:57.549 --> 00:02:03.070
Because at the end of the day it’s their
personality, it’s their talent, it’s their

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:07.780
signature in the world that is going to win
the day.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:13.750
An agent can only open a door, make an introduction,
set the table.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:18.730
But the writer or the actor or whomever, has
to walk into the room (literally and metaphorically)

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.090
and win the day.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:25.170
It has to be their vision, their voice, it
has to be their style, it has to be their

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:30.530
personality and energy that seduces the Universe
into “Yeah!

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.420
I want to play with you.”

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:41.270
We’re going to make your dream come true
because what you bring with you, not because

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:47.720
your agent said X or your manager did Y, that’s
not the truth.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:51.230
The truth is they just opened a door, which
by the way, you could have opened on your

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:57.709
own had you understood that you could have
opened it on your own.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:03.000
But the talent can’t just be the talent.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.860
The talent has to understand (even if it’s
not about how many hours a day they invest

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:11.120
on the business side of their life.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:12.700
It’s deeper than that.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.269
It’s an understanding that I am going to
will this into being.

00:03:17.269 --> 00:03:20.150
I am going to will people into my life who
want to help me.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.069
I am going to will new relationships into
my life.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:26.909
I am going to take action that pays dividends.

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:31.930
Film Courage: So if you had a performer, writer
(what have you) in your [office] chair and

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:36.849
they are sort of slumped down and saying to
you “You know, this just isn’t working.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.569
I have this agent and manager and they’re
not sending me out.

00:03:39.569 --> 00:03:43.720
Or they’re not whatever…It’s “THEY”
We’re putting the blame on THEY, the other

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:44.790
person.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:45.790
What would you say to them?

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:49.519
Gary W. Goldstein: Make them wrong!

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:51.780
Show them how it gets done.

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.510
You want to complain about your agent and
your manager not getting you auditions or

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:58.409
whatever else it happens to be, great.

00:03:58.409 --> 00:03:59.719
Show them how to kick up some dust.

00:03:59.719 --> 00:04:01.680
Get yourself the audition.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.349
It’s not okay to sit home and complain.

00:04:04.349 --> 00:04:09.860
You know, the glass isn’t half empty, ever,
ever, ever, ever.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:11.640
We’re all allowed our moment.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:17.799
We’re allowed to have that one day or (preferably)
that one hour [to complain], right?

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:23.600
Then you have to dust yourself off and say
success is about moving on with it.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:29.550
And if other people aren’t getting it done
for you, then you’ve got to motivate them.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:32.530
And the best way to motivate someone is to
show them what they’re not doing by doing

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.530
it yourself.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:33.543
Question for the Viewers: What’s one thing
you did for your career today?

